menu "Gate regional settings"

choice GATE_MAINS_FREQ_DEFAULT
    bool "Default mains frequency (regional)"
    default GATE_MAINS_AUTO
    help
        Selects the initial value of gate_config.mains_freq on first boot.
        Can always be changed at runtime via NVS / web UI / console ("cfg").
        AUTO measures the zero-cross period and latches 50 or 60 Hz.

    config GATE_MAINS_AUTO
        bool "Auto-detect from zero-cross (safe for any region)"
    config GATE_MAINS_50HZ
        bool "50 Hz (RU/EU/CIS, most of Asia, AU/NZ)"
    config GATE_MAINS_60HZ
        bool "60 Hz (US/CA/MX, JP-west, SA, KR/TW)"
endchoice

choice GATE_CT_DEFAULT
    bool "Default current-sensor variant (first boot)"
    default GATE_CT_ZMCT
    help
        Initial value of gate_config.ct_sensor. DECISION 2026: ZMCT103C
        split-core CT is the PRIMARY sensor (galvanic isolation, zero
        offset drift, cheap; AC-only is fine for pinch/RMS protection and
        battery telemetry was dropped by decision). The Hall front end
        (ACS712/ACS723 class) stays selectable as legacy bring-up fallback
        (devkit / variant-A footprint on custom board v1). Runtime-
        selectable via NVS / web UI / console ("ct") — this choice only
        sets the first-boot default.

    config GATE_CT_ZMCT
        bool "ZMCT103C transformer (burden 2x22R, K_eff=22 mV/A, AC-only) [PRIMARY]"
    config GATE_CT_HALL
        bool "Hall ratiometric (ACS712-30A class, K=66 mV/A, DC-capable) [legacy fallback]"
endchoice

endmenu
